Deterministic numbering for Manifold's parallel level set.

Applies to https://github.com/elalish/manifold at 7c86359 (src/sdf.cpp). Modified by the
GeometryEngine authors, 2026-10-22; the change is the whole of the diff below, and the patched
source carries a comment saying so (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)).

Manifold::LevelSet's parallel passes hand out vertex numbers with AtomicAdd and append triangles
in whatever order their threads run, and everything after them - halfedges, topology cleanup,
sorting - depends on that order, so the same field meshed twice could come back with different
geometry. The positions and the triangles' vertex sets do not depend on thread order. Each vertex
is given a key from where it was made - its grid point and the edge (0-6) or the grid point itself
(7) - and once the triangles are built, vertices are renumbered in key order and triangles rotated
(keeping their winding) and sorted. The sequential and parallel meshers then give the same mesh,
on every call.

Apply from the Manifold checkout:  git apply <this file>

